    "group": "201-300",
    "title": "Delete Node in a Linked List",
    "workload": "build an 8,000-node index-pool list once, then 7,000 cycles; each cycle relinks the pool into one list and then repeatedly sweeps it deleting every other node by the O(1) copy-successor-and-splice rule until one node is left, summing the survivors after every sweep; sink is a rolling 30-bit polynomial hash of those per-sweep sums, a loop-carried dependency so the punch loop is sequential by construction. The delete is two dependent loads and two stores per node and the survivor walk is a pointer chase, so neither vectorizes; the per-cycle relink is the one vectorizable loop and is ~1/6 of the memory traffic",
